@page "/usernameless/{handler?}"
@{
    Layout = "_Layout.cshtml";
}

<div class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <h1 class="title is-1">Scenario: Passkey sign-in (usernameless)</h1>
        <div class="content">
            <p>This is the closest thing to a real passkey experience: no username, no password. Registering requires the resident key (discoverable credential) option, so the credential itself carries enough information for the authenticator to find it. Signing in, the user picks their account from whatever passkeys their device or credential manager offers &mdash; there is nothing to type.</p>
            <p>Note: "passwordless" means no password is sent over the internet or stored in a database. A PIN or biometric might still be used locally, by the authenticator, to unlock the passkey.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="notification is-danger" id="notSupportedWarning" style="display:none">
            Please note: Your browser does not seem to support WebAuthn yet. <a href="https://caniuse.com/#search=webauthn" target="_blank">Supported browsers</a>
        </div>

        <div class="columns">
            <div class="column is-4">

                <h3 class="title is-3">Register user</h3>
                <form action="/usernameless" method="post" id="register">
                    @*<div class="field">
                            <label class="label">Username</label>
                            <div class="control has-icons-left has-icons-right">
                                <input class="input" type="text" placeholder="abergs" name="username" required>
                                <span class="icon is-small is-left">
                                    <i class="fas fa-user"></i>
                                </span>
                            </div>
                        </div>*@

                    <div class="field">
                        <label class="label">Display name</label>
                        <div class="control has-icons-left has-icons-right">
                            <input class="input" type="text" placeholder="Anders Åberg" name="displayName">
                            <span class="icon is-small is-left">
                                <i class="fas fa-user"></i>
                            </span>
                        </div>
                        <p class="help">Optional - but recommended.</p>
                    </div>

                    <div class="field">
                        <div class="control">
                            <button class="button is-link">Register user</button>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </form>
            </div>
            <div class="column is-2"></div>
            <div class="column is-4">

                <h3 class="title is-3">Sign in</h3>


                <form action="/usernameless" method="post" id="signin">
                    @*<div class="field">
                            <label class="label">Username</label>
                            <div class="control has-icons-left has-icons-right">
                                <input class="input" type="text" placeholder="abergs" name="username" required>
                                <span class="icon is-small is-left">
                                    <i class="fas fa-user"></i>
                                </span>
                            </div>
                        </div>*@


                    <div class="field">
                        <div class="control">
                            <button class="button is-link">Sign in</button>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </form>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>


<div class="section">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="content">
            <h1 class="title is-2">Explanation: Passkey sign-in with FIDO2</h1>
            <p>
                A passkey is a discoverable WebAuthn credential: one the authenticator can find on its own, without the Relying Party naming it by ID first. That's what makes typing a username unnecessary here, and it's what the resident key / <code>residentKey</code> option requests at registration.
                The flow is visualized in the figure below.
            </p>
            <img src="~/images/scenario3.png" alt="figure visualizing username and challenge sent together with assertion" />
            <p>The Relying Party can still ask for user verification (PIN or biometrics) by setting <code>UserVerification</code> to required &mdash; two factors in one gesture, since unlocking the passkey both proves possession of the private key and verifies the person. Setting it to discouraged instead checks only user presence, minimizing the interaction needed to sign in.</p>

            <p>
                Read the source code for this demo here: <a href="@Url.ToGithub("Demo/wwwroot/js/usernameless.register.js")">usernameless.register.js</a> and <a href="@Url.ToGithub("Demo/wwwroot/js/usernameless.login.js")">usernameless.login.js</a> &mdash; these set the options that make this scenario what it is. The ceremony they run is shared by every scenario and lives in <a href="@Url.ToGithub("Demo/wwwroot/js/webauthn.js")">webauthn.js</a>.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<script src="~/js/webauthn.js"></script>
<script src="~/js/usernameless.register.js"></script>
<script src="~/js/usernameless.login.js"></script>